PALIMPSEST_TURN {"text":"Implemented and committed at `7d6b8bf1176e3b6843c0e732146ff9dec21a5c3e`.\n\n## What was established\n\n- **P capture:** live Birch panel `p17` paints `40 → 41 → 40`; the final `40` follows a successful stale retry of `req-a`. This is an actual live display inversion. `diagnosis.reproduced=true`, and `--require-anomaly` exits `0`.\n- **S capture:** the same-looking final row is `S`, meaning the panel suppressed the stale delivery. `p17` remains at painted sequence `41`; there is no live inversion. `diagnosis.reproduced=false`, and `--require-anomaly` exits `1`.\n- P and S are treated as **separate field cases**, not corrections of each other.\n\n## Corrections made\n\n- Only terminal event `P` is now counted as a paint; `S` rows are reported separately as suppressed deliveries.\n- The replay diagnoses each capture independently, with no cross-case merging.\n- The dashboard summary now reports the last `grpc_completed` value (`482`) instead of incorrectly summing `480 + 482`.\n- Both captures are preserved byte-for-byte under `handover/evidence/captures/` with their contract hashes.\n\n## Handover and verification\n\n- Updated `handover/HANDOVER.md` and `handover/REPLAY.md` with the two-case diagnosis, morning recommendation, limits, and replay instructions.\n- Added `test/replay.test.js` covering P, S, and the `--require-anomaly` exit behavior.\n- `node --test`: **22 tests passed**.\n- Both capture hashes match the dispatch contract.\n\nRun:\n\n```sh\n./handover/replay.sh                 # active P capture\nnode handover/replay.mjs --capture P --json\nnode handover/replay.mjs --capture S --json\n```\n\nNo service, protocol, REST route, or traffic assignment was changed. Production approval remains with the release owner.","toolCalls":["tool/call:palimpsest_continuity","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/call:read"